~ start
Monk: How lovely!
Plooy: You… [wait=1]You can see Plooy?
Monk: Yes. I have been in this place for… [speed=0.2]eons…
Monk: And to you, “eons” are nothing more than a fickle of dust.
Plooy: Time does not seem to work here as intended.
Plooy: Has Plooy’s undoing caused more rifts in time?
Monk: No… you have done the right things. It is “I” [speed=0.5]who stopped time in this stream.
Plooy: But why? Why would you do that?
Monk: “Time”, is a river with many eddies…
Monk: The more you move forward in it… the more it pushes against itself.
Plooy: A… disagreement?
Monk: Exactly. For every right choice you make, there exists another Plooy — in another timeline — who made the wrong one.
Monk: You must tread carefully. Plooy must not repeat those mistakes… and “I” must not make any more wrong decisions.

