Plooy: You’re… [speed=0.2]ME?
Plooy: These statues… Plooy recognizes them. They look like the lives Plooy has touched.
Plooy: Monk, what are these? What purpose do they serve?
Monk: They are echoes. Nothing more.
Plooy: Echoes of what?
Monk: Of steps taken… and steps yet to be taken…
Plooy: Plooy does not understand.
Monk: You’re not meant to. Not yet.

Plooy: Are we… [speed=0.5]the cause of the time splits?
Monk: [speed=0.5]That is correct. [speed=1.0]“I” must not let you go any further. The heart of time and its pillars must remain like insects in amber.
Plooy: We both know that our mistakes will create unpleasant consequences. But even so… we must keep going!
Monk: Very well. But I must remind you, [speed=0.2]“time” [speed=1.0]will not always be in your favor.

